From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Opt into CN name constraints with OpenSSL 4.1

curl still matches CN-only certificates itself. OpenSSL 4.1 no longer checks
DNS name constraints on those names unless the application explicitly enables
subject checking, allowing a constrained CA to authenticate an unrelated host.
Keep the certificate chain checks consistent with curl's hostname fallback.
This also checks CN constraints on certificates that have a SAN.

--- a/lib/vtls/openssl.c
+++ b/lib/vtls/openssl.c
@@ -3944,6 +3944,15 @@
    * We then explicitly check the result and may try alternatives like
    * Apple's SecTrust for verification. */
   SSL_CTX_set_verify(octx->ssl_ctx, SSL_VERIFY_NONE, NULL);
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x40100000L
+  {
+    X509_VERIFY_PARAM *param = SSL_CTX_get0_param(octx->ssl_ctx);
+    /* curl's CN fallback also needs OpenSSL's DNS name constraints. */
+    X509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_hostflags(param,
+      X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags(param) |
+      X509_CHECK_FLAG_ALWAYS_CHECK_SUBJECT);
+  }
+#endif
 
   /* Enable logging of secrets to the file specified in env SSLKEYLOGFILE. */
 #if !defined(HAVE_KEYLOG_UPSTREAM) && defined(HAVE_KEYLOG_CALLBACK)
